/*
 * Rules that can't be written yet: the old StyleFortress rules that have no SUIL counterpart.
 * This file has no rules, it is only a list.
 */

/* ---- from buttons ---- */
/* ---------- Rules that can't be written yet ----------
 *
 * ProgressButton (type): Prop(ProgressButton.StylePropertyForeground, StyleBoxFlat black 20% alpha)
 *   -> the foreground of a progress button, there is no SUIL property for it.
 *
 * TreeMenuButton: StylePropertyMarkerTexture (tree_menu_button_marker.png, ..._hovered.png when hovered)
 *   and StylePropertyMarkerColor (gold-button-color-default)
 *   -> the marker of a tree menu button, there is no SUIL property for it.
 *
 * MenuButton (type): the colors are the same as rf-button, a Suil counterpart of MenuButton is a RfButton.
 *
 * OptionButton (type): the Suil replacement is RfOptionButton, a RfButton, so rf-button styles it.
 *
 * Label.StylePropertyAlignMode (Label.AlignMode.Center) of rf-button and `.option-button` is text-align: center.
 */

/* ---- from unsupported.suil ---- */
/*
 * Rules that can't be written yet.
 *
 * ---- The control has no Suil counterpart (a rule selects it by type) ----
 *
 * CheckBox: BoxContainer.Class(checkBox).Prop(separation, 10)
 *   -> the 10px between the box and the label; RfCheckBox is not a RfBoxContainer, so there is no `gap`.
 *
 * TabContainer
 *   panel:         tabcontainer_panel.png, patch margin 2, content margin top 2
 *   active tab:    background dark-forest, content margin horizontal 5
 *   inactive tab:  background graphite-black, content margin horizontal 5
 *
 * ProgressBar
 *   background:    dark_panel_light_thin_border.png, patch margin 1, expand margin 1, content margin vertical 14.5
 *   foreground:    background dark-good, content margin vertical 14.5
 *
 * Slider (+ ColorableSlider)
 *   background:    slider_fill.png modulated graphite-black, patch margin 12
 *   foreground:    slider_outline.png modulated dark-good, patch margin 12
 *   grabber:       slider_grabber.png modulated button-color-default, patch margin 12
 *   fill:          slider_fill.png modulated good (slider-red: bad, slider-green: good, slider-blue: blue,
 *                  slider-white: rim-silver; they were Red, Green, Blue and White)
 *
 * ItemList
 *   background:               dark-forest (transparent-item-list and transparent-background-item-list: transparent)
 *   item background:          dark-forest, content margin 2px 4px (transparent-item-list: transparent)
 *   disabled item background: graphite-black
 *   selected item background: bright-green
 *
 * Tree
 *   background:    dark-forest
 *   selected item: graphite-black, content margin left 4
 *
 * Placeholder
 *   panel:         placeholder.png, tiled, patch margin 19, expand margin -5
 *
 * FancyBack
 *   edge color gold-fortress, texture stripeback.png with the TiledTexture shader;
 *   none-back: transparent texture; wooden-back: wooden_back.png
 *
 * FancyTree
 *   icon color and line color: gold-fortress
 *
 * Tooltip (the engine control)
 *   panel: the same box as .tooltip-box
 *
 * ---- There is no SUIL property for it ----
 *
 * PdaSettingsButton / PdaProgramItem (StylePropertyBgColor, StylePropertyFgColor):
 *   normal:   bg #25252A (PdaSettingsButton.NormalBgColor), fg PdaSettingsButton.EnabledFgColor
 *   hover:    bg PdaSettingsButton.HoverColor
 *   pressed:  bg PdaSettingsButton.PressedColor
 *   disabled: bg NormalBgColor, fg PdaSettingsButton.DisabledFgColor
 *   (the colors are constants of the controls, not of the sheet)
 */

/* ---- from panel ---- */
/*
 * Rules that can't be written yet:
 *
 * Placeholder (type), TabContainer, ProgressBar, Slider, ColorableSlider, ItemList, Tree,
 * FancyTree: see the list above (input).
 */

/* ---- from text ---- */
/*
 * Rules that can't be written yet:
 *
 * RichTextLabel.LabelSubText (the paper variant of label-sub-text: font 10, color graphite-black)
 *   The Label and the RichTextLabel had different rules for the same class, selected by the control type. Now the
 *   type is gone, so the paper text has to get its own class (e.g. paper-label-sub-text).
 *
 * ItemStatus of a RichTextLabel (margin 0 0 0 -6 instead of 0 0 2px 4px): needs a class of its own too.
 *
 * Popup messages (PopupMessageSmall, ...Caution, ...Medium, ...Large): StyleFortress only declares the names.
 */
